  <div class="hd-tag">CEE 340 &middot; Advanced Foundation Engineering &middot; Ch. 7</div>
  <h1>Lateral Earth Pressure</h1>
  <p class="hd-sub">Every retaining wall, basement wall, and sheet pile lives or dies by one question: how hard is the soil behind it pushing? The answer isn't a fixed number — it depends on which way the wall moves. That single idea is this whole chapter.</p>
  <div class="hd-pills">
    <span class="pill">At-Rest (K&#8320;)</span>
    <span class="pill">Active (K<sub>a</sub>)</span>
    <span class="pill">Passive (K<sub>p</sub>)</span>
    <span class="pill">Rankine &amp; Coulomb</span>
  </div>
</header>

